    "venueExpansion": "Phase 14.7: 16 anchor venues from Phase 7 nightlife/food engines promoted to BIZ entries. 171 total venues exist in engine pools; these 16 are the permanent base establishments across 11 neighborhoods.",
    "civicEstablishments": "S334: INIT-001/002/003/005/007 minted as BIZ-00094..00098 (Business_Ledger) so civic programs employ their own directors instead of parking at City of Oakland. Keyword rules route future citizens naming these programs.",
    "categoryFix": "S335: Professional -> SELF_EMPLOYED (private practice is honest for vets/CPAs/agents/attorneys); 2041-Specific default REMOVED (no one employer fits the range) with per-role keyword rules routing the placeable specialists. Only Tech & Innovation still defaults to BIZ-00030.",
    "engine83Tail": "S348 (Kimi): Task 7 tail rules — 61 keyword rules from a 6-seat agent fan-out over 293 unmatched citizens, lead-reviewed. Civic/public-safety cluster routed by exact role (DEPUTY CHIEF/INTERNAL AFFAIRS -> BIZ-00024, DISTRICT ATTORNEY/PUBLIC DEFENDER -> BIZ-00022, FIRE CHIEF/EMS -> BIZ-00023), trades -> BIZ-00020, food-service -> BIZ-00044 (Line Cook precedent), creative/gig roles -> SELF_EMPLOYED. Rejected as unearned guesses, left blank: Janitor, Security Guard, Mover, Mechanic, Delivery driver, Maintenance tech, generic Athlete/Driver/Office worker (no honest employer exists in the ledger). Specific-before-generic ordering matters: Climate Modeling before Model; West Oakland Community Center before Community Director.",
    "engine83Close": "S349: close-out pass on the post-Kimi tail (119). Script gains a no-employment skip class (student/retired/hall-of-famer/resident ~55 rows — blank employer is correct, they are not failed matches); Health Officer -> BIZ-00015 (county public health sits with Alameda Health); informal-economy operators (Booky, Drug Dealer, Organized Crime) -> SELF_EMPLOYED. Remaining unmatched are Kimi's ruled-blank generic-service roles plus role/econ-drift rows — blank with reason, per the plan's 'blank is honest' rule."
  },
